1
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,720
Good evening!

2
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:43,960
I bought quite a bit of groceries today

3
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:56,000
It's been raining a lot these days and the humidity is very high

4
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:06,800
Because of this, washing my hands after returning home feels extra good

5
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:22,240
The presence of daffodils at the grocery store is a clear indication that Spring is just around the corner

6
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:36,560
Flowers are one of those small things that can make me happy for days

7
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:55,520
Poppies are my favorite flowers ~ they bloom like living masterpieces, each one a true work of art

8
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:22,360
I like to quickly "prepare" my groceries once I get home

9
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:45,880
Cutting the butter into small pieces will make it so much more convenient to use when you need it

10
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:57,440
However, I don't use separators between pieces (I am a "little" frugal in that regard haha (⸝⸝ᵕᴗᵕ⸝⸝))

11
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:08,440
As long as you leave a bit of space between the pieces, they won't stick together even if they fall

12
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:24,640
For vegetables, I like to clean them and then let them dry before storing them in the fridge

13
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:36,440
Dirt trapped in the vegetables can carry bacteria which may lead to contamination

14
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:57,760
Berries are Koko's favourite fruit, so I usually buy a lot and wash them all at once

15
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:14,560
I give them a quick rinse and then soak them in baking soda water for 15 minutes

16
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:24,720
Baking soda helps to remove dirt, pesticides, and other residues effectively

17
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:54,520
You can leave the berries to air dry, but it usually takes really long, so I like to use a salad spinner

18
00:04:57,960 --> 00:05:07,400
I promise it's not just because the salad spinner would otherwise sit unused... 𓏗-𓏗

19
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:48,840
For proteins, I like to remove them from their packaging as soon as I get home

20
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:58,560
It's a habit my mother-in-law taught me long ago, and it really stuck with me

21
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:11,120
She mentioned that this helps reduce the chances of plastic leaching into the food, and I've followed her advice ever since

22
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:26,880
Every Friday afternoon, 🐢 takes 🐨 out to play, so I have some time for myself before dinner

23
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:40,920
I've been loving rooibos and rose tea lately

24
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:51,040
I think they complement each other perfectly ~

25
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:10,240
The aroma is very delicate, sweet, and soothing ~

26
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:37,000
Pouring it into the biggest mug I have 😅

27
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:48,880
The flavour is so rich and mellow at the same time, and so comforting ~

28
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:08,720
I brewed extra tea to enjoy later

29
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:19,680
We've been eating out a lot lately with relatives visiting, so I've really been craving 'home food'

30
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:28,480
I reckon 'home food' is different for everyone, but for me, it’s either pasta or rice with stir-fried dishes

31
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:37,480
I guess it’s a blend of my Chinese heritage and being born and raised in Italy

32
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:47,880
What's your version of 'home food'?

33
00:08:54,240 --> 00:09:01,280
Tonight, I'm going to be making Chinese style food ~

34
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:09,640
Boiling the pork with a bit of ginger for 5 minutes helps to remove any unpleasant odors

35
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:21,520
For the sauce, I'm using 1/2 tbsp tamari, 1 tbsp oyster sauce, and 1/2 tbsp sugar

36
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:37,680
Fry the ginger in a bit of oil until fragrant

37
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:47,040
Then add in your protein of choice and fry until golden brown

38
00:09:53,920 --> 00:10:00,960
Finally, add the vegetables and sauce

39
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:10,280
Many combinations of proteins and vegetables can work with this recipe

40
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:24,360
(Can you tell Koko came home? 😆)

41
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:34,360
The second dish (Koko's favourite dish) is a child's favourite

42
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:44,800
I have so many memories of eating steamed eggs mixed with rice when I was a kid

43
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:52,040
Typically, you'd sift the eggs like I'm doing here to achieve the smoothest texture

44
00:10:53,280 --> 00:11:00,320
However, since we're at home (and eggs are expensive), I just use them as they are

45
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:09,840
I like to steam the mixture for 5 minutes before adding my toppings and steaming for 6 more minutes

46
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:18,200
(I got distracted and steamed them for 8 minutes before adding the toppings, but it was fine)

47
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:37,560
Lastly, I'll boil some romaine lettuce

48
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:46,840
In reality, I've been multitasking all the dishes, but I think it's easier to watch this way? 😆

49
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:55,840
The romaine lettuce is ready to be served after about 30 seconds

50
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:14,080
I'm going to make a quick sauce with a bit of garlic, soy sauce, and sugar

51
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:54,720
Serving dinner with some mixed purple rice ~

52
00:12:58,080 --> 00:13:05,120
🐢&amp;🐨:"Thanks Mamma"

53
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:13,920
🐨:"Steamed egg, steamed egg 🎶"

54
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:25,760
It's so delicious ~ Rice killers for sure

55
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:51,760
After dinner, it's time to get Koko ready for bed

56
00:13:52,960 --> 00:14:00,000
Lately, we've been showering together for efficiency

57
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:12,640
It also makes story time cosier and more enjoyable for the both of us since we can cuddle together ~

58
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:22,040
🐻:"Why is he happy?" 🐨:"Because he ate so much food!" 😆

59
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:29,880
🐨:"He ate lots of rice! and steamed eggs!"

60
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:41,200
We used to read the same books to her when she was a baby, but in a very different manner

61
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:50,880
These days, we talk about why the characters may be feeling a certain way

62
00:14:53,840 --> 00:15:00,880
🐨:"We can help her put on a bandaid and she'll feel happy!"

63
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:14,160
After reading some stories, we usually cuddle for a few more minutes before she sleeps in her own bed

64
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:34,080
After hearing much about the benefits of red light, I recently bought a red light mask 👍

65
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:43,360
I'm usually very good at taking it slow, but there are 2 times where I can't!

66
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:51,080
When brushing my teeth and doing a mask 😆 I feel like I have to keep myself busy

67
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:59,880
I purchased a brush cleaner from Amazon and I thought I'd use this time to clean my brushes

68
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:09,560
When did you last wash your brushes? I don't remember the last time I washed mine..

69
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:21,120
I added a bit (too much) of makeup brush cleaning solution

70
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:31,800
The water is turning murky just from dipping the brush 🙂

71
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:44,240
This is actually incredibly fun and, most importantly, very fast!

72
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:57,600
There's still some foam residue, so I rinse it off and then spin it dry

73
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:16,320
It's actually very dry and fluffy after spinning ~

74
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:25,040
And it also comes with a spot to air dry and different attachments

75
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:34,280
I'm very happy with this purchase ! (And so is my skin! Haha )

76
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:07,680
I'm going to prepare yeast waffles for tomorrow's breakfast

77
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:16,320
Combine 190g flour, 4g yeast, 80g milk, 1 egg, 35g of sugar, and a bit of vanilla extract

78
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:26,080
Once the dough is formed, add in 30g of butter and combine

79
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:39,080
Cover and store in the fridge overnight

80
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:55,520
From 9 to 10 it's usually time for 🐢and I to catch up on our day

81
00:18:57,760 --> 00:19:04,800
It's basically the only hour we have for the two of us haha

82
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:16,280
We enjoy some tea and toast to the fact that we did a great job today once again! 😆

83
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:41,600
I divided the dough into 6 parts to make 6 waffles

84
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:49,160
Yeast waffles are so cute and fluffy ✨

85
00:19:55,560 --> 00:20:02,600
I'm going to top the waffles with some greek yoghurt

86
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:11,680
If you add some matcha powder into the yoghurt, you'll get a delicious matcha sauce !

87
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:38,240
Time to make it pretty ~

88
00:20:53,400 --> 00:21:00,440
The weather calls for an iced latte ☺️

89
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:10,520
It feels like I'm at a cafe ☕️

90
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:23,520
Waffles go very well with coffee

91
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:39,560
I hope you enjoyed watching this video as much as I enjoyed making it

